From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:06:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give H.E. the reduced BBM networks as SBML, like the original
 BBM runs

bsaf.jar numbers the CNF variables alphabetically for SBML but in hash order
for .bnet, and bdd_minisat_all is very sensitive to that order (BBM model_004:
about 1 GB from SBML, over 9 GB from .bnet, for the same clauses). The
original BBM runs read the biodivine SBML, so bnet_to_sbml.py writes an SBML
copy of each reduced BBM network and run_benchmarks.py --reduced gives it to
H.E.; an earlier H.E. log from the .bnet is kept as *.bnet.log.superseded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SsRhASNAkZUiX2xuLVAZY
